# Description:
# ------------
# The git-default-branch script automatically detects and outputs the name of the
# default branch for the current Git repository, regardless of whether it is
# named main, master, or a custom branch.
#
# This allows automated workflows and other Git scripts to reliably identify the
# primary branch of a local repository without requiring manual specification or
# hardcoded branch names.
